# --- Pipeline intermediate data ---
# Per-cycle stage output is bulky and must not enter git history, but the
# cross-phase cycle state (cycle.json) MUST be committed so a later scheduled
# run can resume a pending batch (AD-11, Story 3.4).
#
# All three lines are required, in this order. The middle line is the one that
# is easy to omit and fatal to omit: git never descends into an excluded
# directory, so a negation for a file inside it can never match. Re-including
# the directories is what lets git reach the file-level negation.
#
# Do NOT simplify to `data/intermediate/*` — under that pattern cycle.json is
# silently ignored and Story 3.4's resume logic breaks with no obvious cause.
data/intermediate/**
!data/intermediate/**/
!data/intermediate/**/cycle.json
# Keeps the directory itself in a fresh clone; without this the stage contract
# has nowhere to write on first run.
!data/intermediate/.gitkeep
# Atomic-write temp files must never be committed, even if a crash leaves one.
data/**/.*.tmp

# data/history/ is deliberately NOT excluded above -- unlike data/intermediate/'s
# bulky per-stage output, this is a small, intentionally-committed cross-cycle
# record (Story 2.7, FR-18): a GitHub Actions runner is ephemeral, so nothing
# survives between cycles unless it is explicitly tracked in git, the same
# reason cycle.json is committed. See pipeline/stages/history.py.

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Node / Astro ---
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
